## 5. Authentication & Security

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor U as User (Mobile/Web)
    participant A as FastAPI
    participant R as Redis
    participant D as PostgreSQL

    U->>A: POST /auth/login {user_id, password}
    A->>D: Verify user + company
    D-->>A: User record + role + company_id
    A->>A: Verify bcrypt password
    A->>A: Generate Access Token (15min) + Refresh Token (7days)
    A->>R: Store refresh token hash
    A-->>U: {access_token, refresh_token}

    U->>A: Any API request + Bearer token
    A->>A: Verify JWT signature + expiry
    A->>A: Extract company_id + role
    A->>D: Query with company_id filter (RLS)
    D-->>A: Data
    A-->>U: Response

    U->>A: POST /auth/refresh {refresh_token}
    A->>R: Validate refresh token
    A-->>U: New access_token
```

**Security Measures:**
- JWT Access Token: **15 minutes** expiry
- Refresh Token: **7 days**, stored in Redis (revocable)
- Passwords: **bcrypt** (cost factor 12)
- Documents (Aadhaar, PAN): stored **encrypted** on ImageKit + signed URLs
- API Rate Limiting: 100 req/min per user
- HTTPS enforced (Nginx + Let's Encrypt)
- CORS: only allowed origins
- SQL Injection: prevented by SQLAlchemy ORM
- Input validation: Pydantic schemas on all endpoints

